          %title Bitopological space
          %h1#bitopological_space Bitopological space
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#separation_axioms_for_topologies"} Separation axioms for topologies
              %li
                %a{:href => "#remarks"} Remarks
              %li
                %a{:href => "#pointfree_analogues"} Pointfree analogues
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_articles"} Related Articles
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+structure"} topological structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            %strong bitopological space
            is simply a set equipped with
            %em two
            topological structures
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{T}, \mathcal{T}^*)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebras"} bialgebras
          %p
            A
            %strong bicontinous map
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            between bitopological spaces that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            with respect to each topological structure.
          %p
            Bitopological spaces and bicontinuous maps form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BiTop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BiTop
          %h2#separation_axioms_for_topologies Separation axioms for topologies
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cl
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
            with respect to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl^*
            denote the closure operator with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}^*
          %p
          #implications.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{T}, \mathcal{T}^*)
              be a bitopological space. Consider the following properties of this space:
            %ol
              %li#regular1
                %p
                  for each point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  there is a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood+base"} neighborhood base
                  consisting of
                  = succeed "-closed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒯
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}^*
              %li#regular2
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
                  and all
                  = succeed "-opens" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  containing
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  there is a
                  = succeed "-closed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒯
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}^*
                  = succeed "-neighborhood" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  such that
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subset U
              %li#coupled1
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Cl
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl^*(O) \subset Cl(O)
                  for each
                  = succeed "-open" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒯
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}^*
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi O
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
              %li#coupled2
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
                  and all
                  = succeed "-neighborhoods" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
