          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %p It is interesting and perhaps surprising that many advanced topological notions can be described using bitopological spaces, even when you would not naively think that there are two topologies around. (At least, that’s my vague memory of what they were good for. I think that this was in some article by Isbell.)
          %h2#pointfree_analogues Pointfree analogues
          %p
            Expressed in the opposite category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                D-frames
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/D-frames"} ?
